### 2.2 US-138026 - HM Import One time (Prior Data Dump)

Confirmed requirements from the story: a new LERETANet import job; the file layout is the attached TPTI layout (AC1); import rules similar to the CHM import; logging, error handling and reconciliation; failures logged with clear messages (AC2); downstream workflows out of scope. The story also says "pipe delimited", which conflicts with the positional layout (Q2).

Expected behaviour once built:

1. The mainframe drops the TPTI file in the configured folder.
2. The job is started manually (one-time load, Q11). The package finds the folder through FPA, loads every record into a staging table, then into the prior-data table.
3. Each rejected record is written to the error log with the file name, row number, raw record and a plain message. Good records are loaded even when other rows fail (Q14).
4. A summary row records file rows, loaded rows, skipped rows and failed rows, and a completion e-mail reports the same counts.
5. The file is archived. The FPA tracking row shows the final status.
6. The linkage sweep for existing Open CHM records runs as the last step (US-138027, N5).

