### 2.3 US-138027 - Prior Data Store and Linkage

Confirmed requirements from the story: a new table for the prior records (AC1); rows are stored even when no CHM record exists yet (AC2); every attribute is kept as received, never modified or overwritten (AC3); the table is independent of the CHM structure (AC4); the model supports linking later (AC5); when a CHM record is imported and matching priors exist, they are linked (AC6); existing CHM records with Open status are checked for priors and linked (AC7); one CHM record can own many prior rows (AC8); linkage never creates duplicate prior rows (AC9); the link key is Agency ID and Tax ID; priors are linked only once for a given Agency ID and Tax ID.

Proposed table outs\_CHM\_PriorData in LASOutsourcing (name to confirm, N11):

| Column group | Columns | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Key | PriorDataID (identity, primary key) | Row identity |
| Raw values, exactly as received | AGENCY\_ID (9), TAX\_ID (50), TAX\_YEAR (4), BILL\_TYPE (1), PAYCODE\_1..4 (1), INSTALL\_1..4 (11), PENALTY\_1..4 (9), PENALTY\_INTEREST (9), SALES\_NUMBER (10), GOOD\_UNTIL\_DATE\_1 and \_2 (8), REDEEM\_AMT\_1 and \_2 (11), UPDATE\_USER (8), UPDATE\_TIMESTAMP (8), ADD\_USER (8), ADD\_TIMESTAMP (8), HANDLE\_MANUAL\_IND (1), FILLER (12) | Meets AC3: nothing altered |
| Typed values for querying | Install\_1..4\_Amt and Penalty\_1..4\_Amt DECIMAL, PenaltyInterest\_Amt DECIMAL, RedeemAmt\_1 and \_2 DECIMAL, GoodUntilDate\_1 and \_2 DATE, UpdateDate and AddDate DATE, TaxIdNormalized VARCHAR(50) | Reporting and matching without re-parsing |
| Load audit | ImportGroupID, SourceFile, RowNumber, LoadTs | Traceability back to the file |
| Linkage | ParentOIR\_ID INT NULL (points at outs\_OpenItems.OIR\_ID), LinkedDate, LinkedBy (PRIOR\_IMPORT or CHM\_IMPORT) | The parent-child relationship (AC5 to AC8) |
| Indexes | (AGENCY\_ID, TaxIdNormalized) including TAX\_YEAR; (ParentOIR\_ID) | Fast matching and fast reads for the UI |

Proposed linkage SP usp\_CHM\_PriorData\_Link, called in two ways:

- Sweep mode (after the prior load, AC7): for every Open CHM record (definition in N3) that has no linked priors, find unlinked prior rows with the same Agency ID and normalized Tax ID and set ParentOIR\_ID. One Open record per parcel is chosen when several exist (N2).
- Single-record mode (inside the CHM import, AC6): called with the OIR\_ID just inserted or updated. Same match, same once-only rule. Already-linked rows are never moved (N4), so re-imports are idempotent (AC9).

Worked examples of the expected behaviour:

1. Prior load finds Agency 220530000, Tax ID 210518000 with three tax years, and an Open CHM item exists for that parcel. Result: three rows stored, all three linked to that item.
2. Prior load finds a parcel with no CHM item. Result: rows stored with ParentOIR\_ID empty. Weeks later the CHM import brings a new item for that parcel. Result: the import links the waiting rows to the new item.
3. The same CHM item is re-imported the next day. Result: nothing changes; the rows stay linked once.

