Assumptions applied unless the team says otherwise:

- New SSIS work lives in the Outsourcing project, uses the project-level LASOutsourcing connection manager, follows the CHM package's OnError and archive pattern, and is deployed to the SSISDB LERETANet/Outsourcing folder with the current environment reference looked up at deployment time.
- All SQL objects go in LASOutsourcing; deployment scripts in SQL/Deployment-Scripts/\<MMDDYYYY>/; test scripts under Documents/LERETANet/Scripts/\<TicketID>/.
- No SSRS, LeretanetCore or LeretaReportsAPI changes.
- The user-entered Prior Information rows and the SPs that save them are not modified.

Decisions needed, by owner:

- Product Owner: N1, N2, N4, N8, N9, N10, N13, Q11, Q13, and the N6 natural key.
- Tech Lead: N3, N5, N11, N12, Q10, Q14.
- Mainframe team: Q2, Q3, Q7, Q9, Q15, Q16.
- Infrastructure or DBA: Q4.

Proposed build order (bottom-up, so each layer is testable before the next):

1. US-138027 table and staging table, plus the deployment and test scripts.
2. US-138026 load SP and summary variant, tested in SSMS with the sample file.
3. US-138027 linkage SP in both modes, tested against seeded Dev CHM items.
4. US-138026 package, FPA row and job; full run in Dev; verify counts, error log, archive.
5. US-138027 hook in usp\_OI\_CHM\_ImportProcess\_OIRecord; regression run of the CHM import in Dev.
6. US-138028 result set in outs\_COP\_LoanDetails\_S, then the page binding and markup.

Deployment sequence per environment: SQL tables, then SPs, then the FPA seed, then the SSIS project, then the job, then the LERETANet web and middle-tier build; the one-time load is started manually after the file is confirmed present.
